// TEST: TreeIdx through a chained alias still refuses (rejects)
// TRAP T1: a structural TypeExpr walk that lacks the TreeIdx arm treats the
// type as ABSENT, and the sneaky case is alias-body laundering -- `type B = A`
// carries the arm into positions the walk never probes. If registerTypeDecl's
// TyTreeIdx arm is missing, B registers as a plain TDIAlias and this program
// typechecks silently, which is the failure this file exists to catch.
